# Scope the published ClawHub skill to the MCP server only — mirrors the npm
# package.json "files" allowlist (which already scopes the npm package).
#
# These stay in git (the Vercel x402-watch dashboard + CI build from them) and
# are never shipped to npm; this file only controls what ClawHub packs, so the
# dashboard and npm package are unaffected.
#
# IMPORTANT: .gitignore syntax — NO inline/trailing comments. A "#" only starts
# a comment at the START of a line, so "web/   # foo" becomes a literal pattern
# that matches nothing. Keep every pattern on its own bare line. (This was the
# bug in the first version of this file: web/ scripts/ python/ .github/ all had
# trailing comments and were therefore NOT excluded.)
#
# clawhub reads .gitignore first, then this file, so node_modules/dist/.env are
# already excluded. Below we drop the non-MCP, higher-scope components the
# security scanner flagged as broader than "subgraph discovery":
web/
scripts/
python/
docs/
.github/
*.parquet
